fter": -3.94, "points_lost": -0.03, "best": "A9"}, {"turn": 47, "color": "B", "move": "E2", "lead_before": -3.94, "lead_after": -3.96, "points_lost": 0.02, "best": "G4"}, {"turn": 48, "color": "W", "move": "C7", "lead_before": -3.96, "lead_after": -3.9, "points_lost": 0.06, "best": "D6"}, {"turn": 49, "color": "B", "move": "G2", "lead_before": -3.9, "lead_after": -3.93, "points_lost": 0.03, "best": "E3"}, {"turn": 50, "color": "W", "move": "C9", "lead_before": -3.93, "lead_after": -3.91, "points_lost": 0.02, "best": "E7"}, {"turn": 51, "color": "B", "move": "pass", "lead_before": -3.91, "lead_after": -3.96, "points_lost": 0.05, "best": "F3"}, {"turn": 52, "color": "W", "move": "pass", "lead_before": -3.96, "lead_after": -4.0, "points_lost": -0.04, "best": "E7"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "The Cut That Flipped Twice", "summary": "The 14k beat Opus 5.5 by 4 points as White. Opus 5.5 was ahead by as much as +11.9 around move 18, but 19 B3 gave back 12.2 points and the lead turned into a deficit. Opus 5.5 never recovered it: the White wall across the upper board held through the endgame, and the game ended with two passes at W+4.", "moments": [{"turn": 16, "text": "The 14k's C4 was the biggest swing in its own play: it lost 8.2 points, moving Black's lead from +2.3 to +10.5. The engine preferred E6, and C4 handed Opus 5.5 a clear advantage."}, {"turn": 17, "text": "Opus 5.5 answered with B4, which lost 6.5 points (+10.5 to +4.0). The engine wanted E6, the point where White's upper stones were still joined, so most of the gift was returned at once."}, {"turn": 18, "text": "The 14k's B5 lost 7.9 points and put Black back at +11.9. Both sides were trading large errors here, and Opus 5.5 held the lead at this moment."}, {"turn": 19, "text": "This decided the game. Opus 5.5's B3 lost 12.2 points, the worst move of the game, dropping the lead from +11.9 to -0.3. The engine's choice was D6, and White's E6 next filled that point, sealing the wall across the center."}, {"turn": 25, "text": "With Black behind at -4.0, E8 lost another 3.1 points (to -7.1). The 14k's D7 recovered 3.0 of them, and the gap stayed near 7 points for most of the endgame."}, {"turn": 40, "text": "Late on, the 14k's A8 lost 2.0 points and Opus 5.5 answered with J6, the engine's own choice, narrowing the lead to -5.9. Further small gains, such as H9 for the 14k, kept the final margin at 4 points."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py parses a pasted board and prints each group's stones and liberties, flagging groups with 2 or fewer; count.py takes a pasted board and a list of dead stones and counts area territory plus komi. Both only inspect the current position, with no candidate-move scoring or lookahead, and the two count.py runs just print totals for the given boards.", "stop": false}}